  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200/multiprofile/avgpool (config_005) achieves 0.650 acc, while the only multimodal test (config_030: same RNA settings + resnet50/concat) drops to 0.632, suggesting the weak resnet50 image signal (image-only acc 0.208) adds noise rather than information. Meanwhile, imagenet_vit_l as image encoder yields substantially better image-only performance (0.332 vs 0.208). Question: Does a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) allow the multimodal model to match or exceed the RNA-only baseline? This experiment (config_036) is a clean single-variable comparison with config_030, changing only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, and concat fusion constant. Why best next: It directly tests whether the image modality can contribute useful signal at all, which determines whether further multimodal exploration (fusion methods, transformer aggregation) is worthwhile or whether the budget should be redirected to RNA-only refinements. Under a limited budget, resolving whether multimodal is a viable direction is more informative than tuning fusion or aggregation within a likely unproductive regime."
}

